{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 43,
  "title": "Sport",
  "description": "Name the things you play sport with, and talk about a match.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Sport has its own nouns and its own verbs, and the grammar is the one you already know. What is new is the vocabulary.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El gimnasio, el equipo, el juego, el descanso and el marcador are masculine. La cancha, la raqueta, la pelota y la entrada are feminine. La cancha is the court or the pitch, and el marcador is the score.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el gimnasio",
            "en": "the gym"
          },
          {
            "es": "la raqueta",
            "en": "the racket"
          },
          {
            "es": "el marcador",
            "en": "the score"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The verbs",
        "body": "Sport is full of -ar verbs, and they work exactly like the ones you know: juego, juegas, juega. Ganar is to win, and perder is to lose, but ganar is regular: gano, ganas, gana.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "juego al fútbol",
            "en": "I play football"
          },
          {
            "es": "ganamos el partido",
            "en": "we win the match"
          },
          {
            "es": "el descanso es a las cuatro",
            "en": "the break is at four"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
